# Entry Main. The paired control of struct_actual_named_unknown_refused: the data declares an input of that name, and
# the named actual is taken into it -- its value is read once, before the call (step 21.7 K2). `Add` has the inputs
# `data` and `other`; `Add\add(data := bump())` runs `add` over `Add`: `bump` counts one call, and the body reads the
# other input of the same data (`other`, 5) and writes it into `Box\q`. The word `data` in code is the data of the
# call, so the supplied value of the input `data` is not read by its name here.
# Norm: the book #structural-call (the names of the members of the actuals denote inputs of the data; a supplied actual
# fills the selected place in a fresh namespace; the source data and code are unchanged).
int: before 0
int: calls 0
int: after 0
fn: bump () int
    node\calls := node\calls + 1
    return: 7
Box:
    int: q 1
end: Box
Add:
    int: data 0
    int: other 5
    add:
        Box\q := other
    end: add
end: Add
Main:
    node\before := 1
    Add\add(data := bump())
    node\after := 2
